---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "PunchOut Solutions for Shopify | Swishtag";
const description = "Enable PunchOut purchasing workflows for Shopify company stores and enterprise buyers.";
const canonical = "https://cms.swishtag.com/platforms/punchout-solutions/";
const robots = "index,follow";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} robots={robots}>
  <link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/generic-page.css" />
  <main><section class="gp-hero"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-kicker">PunchOut Solutions</div><h1>Make Shopify work with enterprise procurement.</h1><p>PunchOut Solutions is Swishtag’s procurement layer for organizations that need buyers to shop a controlled catalog while purchasing through their existing procurement process.</p><div class="gp-actions"><a class="gp-btn primary" href="/book-demo/">Book a demo ↗</a><a class="gp-btn secondary" href="/solutions/">Explore solutions</a></div></div></section><section class="gp-section"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-section-head"><h2>PunchOut should remove friction, not create another portal.</h2><p>The goal is a clean buying journey for the end user and a controlled procurement path for the enterprise team.</p></div><div class="gp-grid"><article aria-label="Open Shop the approved catalog" class="gp-card st-clickable-card" data-card-href="/book-demo/?service=punchout-solutions" role="link" tabindex="0"><small>BUYER EXPERIENCE</small><h3>Shop the approved catalog</h3><p>Let buyers browse the storefront experience they understand while keeping procurement controls in place.</p><a href="/book-demo/?service=punchout-solutions">Discuss your buyer flow →</a></article><article aria-label="Open Return the cart" class="gp-card st-clickable-card" data-card-href="/book-demo/?service=punchout-solutions" role="link" tabindex="0"><small>PROCUREMENT</small><h3>Return the cart</h3><p>Pass selected items back into the buyer’s procurement workflow for approval and purchase.</p><a href="/book-demo/?service=punchout-solutions">Map the workflow →</a></article><article aria-label="Open Central control" class="gp-card st-clickable-card" data-card-href="/book-demo/?service=punchout-solutions" role="link" tabindex="0"><small>OPERATIONS</small><h3>Central control</h3><p>Use a repeatable integration pattern across company-store programs instead of rebuilding each connection from scratch.</p><a href="/book-demo/?service=punchout-solutions">See the approach →</a></article></div></div></section><section class="gp-section alt"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-split"><div><h2>What this page will cover</h2></div><div class="gp-list"><div>Buyer launches the approved storefront from procurement.</div><div>Buyer selects products, quantities and options.</div><div>Cart data returns to the procurement system.</div><div>The approved order follows the organization’s purchasing process.</div></div></div></div></section><section class="gp-section"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-cta"><div><h2>Have a workflow that does not fit off-the-shelf software?</h2><p>Show us the current process. We can help identify the simplest Shopify, integration, or automation approach before you commit to a larger build.</p></div><a class="gp-btn" href="/book-demo/">Book a demo ↗</a></div><p class="gp-note">This page is connected and launch-ready. Detailed sales copy, proof, screenshots and SEO depth can be expanded in the next content pass.</p></div></section></main>
</BaseLayout>
